Training Expiration Notification Enhancement – Status Update

We have completed the development and initial validation of the dynamic training-expiration notification enhancement in SailPoint IIQ.

Existing Rules and Task Reviewed (Baseline):

* Notification Rule: PGE-Rule-RuleExecutor-TrainingExpirationNotification
* Training Data Library: SAP Training Table Rule Library
* Training Policy Library: SAP Training Policy Rule Library
* Email Template: PGE-EmailTemplate-Training-Warning
* Existing Task: Test- NERC Training Expiration Notification
* Task Type: Notify Users of Expiring Training

Enhanced Rule and Task Used for Testing:

* Dynamic Notification Rule: PGE-Rule-RuleExecutor-TrainingExpirationNotification-Dynamic
* TEST Task: Test- NERC Training Expiration Notification (updated to reference the dynamic rule)

Work Completed:

* Reviewed the existing NERC training notification rule, associated SAP training libraries, entitlement dependency logic, email template, and task configuration to understand the existing notification process.
* Enhanced the notification logic to dynamically identify applicable training courses from the training database instead of maintaining individual course IDs in the task configuration.
* Implemented notification filtering for 30, 15, and 7 days before training expiration.
* Successfully validated dynamic training-course discovery, user identification, identity correlation, and training-dependent entitlement evaluation.
* Validated the existing email notification behavior in TEST, including standard training reminders and conditional access-revocation warnings.
* Successfully executed the enhanced dynamic rule through the TEST TaskDefinition in scan-only mode. The task completed successfully, identifying 2 users across 2 training courses, with no processing errors reported in the earlier diagnostic and no emails sent during task execution.

Current Status:

Development and initial scan-only validation completed successfully. The enhanced rule is functioning through the existing SailPoint notification task framework.

Next Steps:

* Perform controlled end-to-end email notification testing using TEST email redirection.
* Validate notification recipients, manager CC, email content, and conditional entitlement-revocation warnings.
* Review task execution performance and complete final UAT validation.
* Proceed with Production deployment following successful validation, approval, and standard change management.



